  "answer": "heron is the odd one out.\n\n\"Network Automation Fundamentals\" (the student lab, not the Instructor Edition) on each cluster:\n\n| cluster | ci_name | scm_ref |\n|---|---|---|\n| condor | netauto.fundamentals | v3.2.0 |\n| heron | netauto.fundamentals | v2.9.4 |\n| kite | netauto.fundamentals | v3.2.0 |\n| puffin | netauto.fundamentals-ng | v3.2.0 |\n\n3 clusters (condor, kite, puffin) build it from v3.2.0 of https://github.com/rhpds/netauto-labs.git. heron's component still points at v2.9.4. Everything else matches across all four: aws, agnosticv path netauto/fundamentals/common.yaml, and the same expected instances.\n\nOn puffin the catalog item is named netauto.fundamentals-ng, so its component lookup has to use that name. Each catalog also lists a separate Instructor Edition item (netauto.fundamentals-instructor). That is a different item and was left out of the comparison.\n"
